Description: Re-locate the info dict after a tracker edit
 BEP 9 peers fetch metadata pieces that get_metadata_piece() reads from the
 .torrent file at info_dict_offset(). That offset was only set while
 parsing, but set_announce_list() rewrites the file, and tracker keys that
 change size before "info" move the info dict, so peers got a window of the
 right length starting at the wrong byte until the daemon restarted.
 tr_torrent_metainfo::update_info_dict_offset() re-parses the rewritten file
 after a successful save and takes its offset, refusing it if the info dict
 hash or size no longer match. Adds
 TorrentMagnetTest.getMetadataPieceAfterTrackerEdit.
 .
 The test hunk is rebased onto Debian's use-system-libs.patch, which moves
 the gtest include; the library change is the upstream commit unchanged.
Author: netravnen <1938389+netravnen@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: other, https://github.com/netravnen/transmission/commit/2c8b37e7e0b91c575c4e29e476387b8705e845c6
Bug: https://github.com/transmission/transmission/issues/9151
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-18
